# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: ec-02-pincer
number: 302
name: Pincer
pool: Ordinary
description: Grapplers face each other across the board with a pit at each one's feet, so every tile on the middle row is somebody's pull target. Pick which one you stand next to.
retired: superseded by ec-02-pincer-v2, which carries the same thesis over connected blocking mass and a question still live on round 3 (D-280). Kept parseable: the replay logs of every run that played it still name this id.
design: Enemy composition 2 — two Grapplers, one on each side, with a pit at each one's feet. Nothing ever starts standing on a hazard; the format writes Open under every spawn letter.

spawn g = Grappler
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..h..BB
  .H.^.BB
  .......
  gO...Og
  .......
  A..^.H.
  AA.h...
